From 27183108a0225c4ed3bdc3750f9fb82c11fee2ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: review <review@example.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:12:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sealed-factory): one network policy, a publish gate that
 runs the whole suite

The published sealed-factory branch had two honesty defects and one policy defect.

Policy: SEALED_NO_NETWORK was honoured by the net.* and github.* tools and by
selfcheck repairs, but not by the model runtime, the gateway or the swarm. With a
provider key in the environment, 'SEALED_NO_NETWORK=1 tools/factory/
sealed_factory_runtime.py run --max-model-calls 4' still POSTed to
api.openai.com; with no keys the component still called api.github.com from the
researcher role's offline step, so the advertised plan mode was not offline.

  * add runtime/netpolicy.py as the single answer: SEALED_NETWORK=off (default),
    local, remote; SEALED_NO_NETWORK=1 always forces off
  * wire it through toolkit, the gateway, the swarm and the sealed runtime
  * default every model-call cap to 0; --allow-network local|remote is the opt-in
  * record skipped network steps/checks instead of failing them, and count them
  * --allow-network on both CLIs; the environment no longer hard-codes 4 calls
  * tests: shell/tests/test_network_policy.py, plus the GitHub, gateway and
    online-model tests now declare the policy they need

Honesty: the publish gate ran 3 of the 10 test files and the branch's own
discovery test imported a module the seal never listed, so 'passed its own tests'
was not true of the published tree - 14 tests failed or errored there. The seal
omitted tools/factory/discover_factories.py, plan_import.json and
repositories.json while keeping the tests that read them.

  * publish gate 4: the whole suite, under SEALED_NETWORK=off
  * gate 6b: the snapshot's own run also runs under SEALED_NETWORK=off
  * include the three missing growth files and list them for removal
  * host-repository assertions skip with the reason on the component-only tree
  * published_environment_judge: real denominator, and report step skips
  * README arithmetic (171-126 is 45, not 19), --model-calls flag in the docs

Verified: 214 tests OK (5 host-repo skips) with the policy off and with
SEALED_NO_NETWORK=1; selfcheck FUNCTIONAL; verify OK; the snapshot run and the
judge pass with 193/193 checks and 1 policy-skipped step; a real local provider
is reached only with --allow-network local.
