+## Network policy
+
+Nothing leaves this machine unless the run is told it may. `SEALED_NETWORK` is `off` by default;
+`local` permits the gateway and local model servers on `127.0.0.1`, and `remote` adds the providers
+and the GitHub API. `--allow-network local|remote` sets it for one run, and `SEALED_NO_NETWORK=1`
+always forces `off` - the air-gapped job's switch cannot be weakened by another variable. The model
+runtime, the gateway, the swarm and the `net.*`/`github.*` tools all read the same policy; the run
+report records the mode and counts the steps the policy skipped instead of failing them.
 
